      "problem": "Which of the following equations have no real solution?\n\nI. $\\sqrt{7-2x}=-2$\n\nII. $\\sqrt{x-3}=-7$\n\nIII. $\\sqrt{6x-2}=5$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that a square root is always positive or zero. So, a radical equation has no real solution if it states that a square root is equal to a negative number.\n\nOf the given equations, only I and II state that a square root is equal to a negative number. Therefore, equations I and II have no real solution.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
